WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.368
In a historic first

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.003
former president of the United States

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.670
and a current

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.005
presidential candidate

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.773
on top of that announced his own

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:07.741
federal indictment.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:08.241
Joining us now

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.510
for their take on this monumental day

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.344
in the history

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.545
of this great republic,

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.247
former Watergate special prosecutor

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.215
Richard Ben-Veniste

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:17.450
and legendary Watergate journalist

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.284
Bob Woodward.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.052
Bob,

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.687
you have interviewed the former

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.656
president extensively in 2019.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.457
He told you

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.826
about a nuclear weapons system

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.128
where he claimed to this.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:31.898
Let's take a listen from your interview

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.167
I have built a weapon system

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:34.901
that nobody has ever

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.669
had in this country before.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.370
We have stuff

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.004
that you haven't

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.706
even seen or heard about.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.041
We have stuff that Putin

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.076
and she have never heard about before.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.179
I mean, that's

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.547
I mean, that's nuts in itself.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.182
But now we know he's been charged with

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.083
with retaining

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.818
these classified documents.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.853
About U.S. nuclear capabilities.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:54.721
And who knows again

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.622
who got access to them?

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.323
Who knows who he told about them.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.192
So this must not actually be surprising

00:00:59.192 --> 00:00:59.893
to you.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.361
No, no.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.831
This indictment and the circumstances

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.966
are a total reflection

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.335
of his personality.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.971
I really think he believes

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.842
democracy is enemy territory

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.944
because it's about other people.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:21.181
And he likes everything to be about him.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:25.485
And I think one of the offshoots of

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.221
this is this is a test

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.324
and a grave crisis.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.426
For the Republican Party.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.462
How is the Republican Party

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.464
going to deal with this?

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.732
We all know lots of Republicans,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.237
many are still law and order Republicans.

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:48.074
And I think they're going to look at this

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.743
and they're going to say, wait a minute,

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:55.248
And this could begin that snowball

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.317
going down the mountain

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:57.951
because it's

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:03.756
so factual, it's so potent And I thought

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.861
Jack Smith, what he did today

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:12.699
when he praised the FBI was so important.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.667
So the Republicans

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:14.901
are going

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.770
to have to go back to Barry Goldwater,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.874
who 50 years ago went to Nixon

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:24.777
and said too many lies, too many crimes.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:25.411
And Nixon

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.780
asked him in a private Oval Office

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.982
meeting with the

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.050
Republican leaders in the House

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.285
and the Senate.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.821
Well, I know I'm going to be impeached.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.690
How will I do in a Senate trial?

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:41.361
Now we need 34 votes to stay in office.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.363
And Goldwater looked at him and said, Mr.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.532
President, and I've counted

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.434
and you have five votes.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.871
And one of them is not my right.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.173
And you don't have mine.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:54.774
Yeah. It's such a great story.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:55.074
Richard,

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.075
I want to get your take on something

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.611
historian Doug Brinkley said today.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:02:59.546
Let's roll that tape.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:02.549
I've always

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.149
thought Ford

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.251
was right to heal the country

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.119
pardoning Nixon.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.120
But in recent years,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.222
I realize it was probably a mistake

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.123
for the reason

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.324
that it encourages

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.526
the arrogance of President Trump,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:13.993
of this

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.029
feeling that he's above the law,

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.431
that the Constitution doesn't matter,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.667
that you can have an authoritarian

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.202
bent to do anything

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.571
you want in the United States.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.171
Do you agree?

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.440
I think the long the long view picture

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.975
of what he's saying is that

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:29.909
if actually there had been

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.778
a trial of Richard Nixon

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.746
and maybe he had gone to the prison

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.216
as many of his coconspirators did,

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.153
then maybe this wouldn't have happened.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.421
But at least

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.156
if the timing was different

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.457
on the pardon,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.393
if President Ford had waited

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:50.964
until we brought charges

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.966
and then Nixon could address

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:53.733
the charges,

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.469
either by accepting a pardon or not,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.271
at least the charges would

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.340
be out there and it would be

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.010
something the public could see.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.714
And I agree that this indictment

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:11.050
really is a reflection of the

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.186
former president's

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:15.521
arrogance, his disdain

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:18.024
for the rule of law.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.693
Which is so repugnant

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.762
to people who have worked

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:26.099
in law enforcement, who have worked

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.468
for the Constitution

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:33.273
bipartisanly over the years

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:37.844
to see this kind of complete disregard

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:42.815
for the rule of law by the president in

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.552
in treating documents which involved

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.054
the national security

00:04:48.054 --> 00:04:51.691
of the United States in this cavalier,

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:55.928
offhanded and totally disrespectful way.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.330
I don't see

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.300
how members of his political party

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:05.038
can accept this as a leader of the party.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.839
So, Bob, you were talking about

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.841
you invoked Goldwater,

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.243
who obviously had been the party,

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.010
the Republican Party's

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.545
nominee for president in 64.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:13.980
So he was the conservative

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.181
standard bearer

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.383
going to Nixon talking to Nixon.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:18.818
And I'm just wondering,

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:22.255
I mean, the the modern incarnation of

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:24.324
that would be Mitt Romney,

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:27.593
very conservative but Donald Trump

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:28.828
doesn't care

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:29.929
what Mitt Romney thinks is

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.764
he wouldn't let him in. Right.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.866
Is there a I mean and to be clear,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.002
he should Mitt Romney is a wise man.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.170
And very conservative.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.106
Is there a Goldwater of today

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:42.041
that that not just Donald Trump,

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:44.210
but Kevin McCarthy would listen to?

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.446
Well, we're going to have to find him

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.980
or the Republican Party

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.084
is going to have to have come to Jesus

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:53.419
meeting with itself and say,

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.588
what are we missing?

00:05:55.588 --> 00:06:00.259
Leadership direction, moral definition,

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:01.828
which has to be

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:04.063
the center of any political party.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:07.233
If I may say, I think this situation

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.837
is a test for Biden and the Democrats.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.806
Also, I think it's really important.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.843
Biden is staying away from this and

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:17.844
so forth. But

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.280
go back 50 years.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.348
The night

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.684
Nixon announced he was

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:26.886
resigning in The Washington Post

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.654
newsroom, Ben Bradlee,

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:29.889
the editor

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:33.092
was running around saying, don't gloat,

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:36.896
no gloating, essential.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:39.198
And I was with Ben.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.466
We were going down

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:43.770
to get something to eat at The Washington

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.672
Post cafeteria, which was just not much.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:50.977
But it was late at night and the elevator

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:54.180
opened and out stepped.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.785
A prominent member of the Kennedy family

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:03.556
and said, Ben, I came here to celebrate.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.661
And Ben almost tackled him, pushing him

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:11.964
back in the elevator and said, no,

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:15.635
no celebration, no gloating.

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.370
And it's very important

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.538
that the Democrats

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:21.307
and those of us in our business

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:26.712
not get in in a celebration mode.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:29.081
Yeah. 1974. Kennedy in Washington.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.483
I think I could figure out who that was.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.752
Maybe it was Sargent Shriver.

00:07:32.752 --> 00:07:33.519
It was Sargent Shriver.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:34.887
He thought it was right.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.722
The Senator Ted Kennedy.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:37.857
Do you agree?

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:38.291
And, you know,

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.692
you brought the Watergate case.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.794
And do you think the Republican Party of

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:43.763
the seventies was different

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.097
from the Republican Party

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.967
today in terms of all that we know

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:49.469
about Nixon

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:52.138
and there was a lot that he did that was

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:55.041
wrong.

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:59.278
And Mean-Spirited and unconstitutional.

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.782
I believe that if he had survived

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:05.651
Watergate wounded but survived,

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:06.819
he was not

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:10.089
an existing threat to our democracy.

00:08:10.857 --> 00:08:12.692
I don't believe the same thing

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:14.160
about Donald Trump.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.396
And I think this is an important step

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.232
for people to consider

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:22.568
how he regarded our national security

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:25.304
in the way he treated these documents.

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:30.042
And the next thing to come is January six

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:34.213
with which was a head on assault against

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:36.349
our democracy.

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:37.283
Two investigations

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:38.251
coming to the fore on that,

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.986
including one from Jack Smith.

00:08:39.986 --> 00:08:41.187
And if I may.

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:42.955
But 50 years ago,

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:44.524
if somebody had said, do you

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:46.292
do you think Richard Nixon is

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:48.961
an existential threat to democracy,

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.129
you would have said yes.

00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:50.963
No, I wouldn't.

00:08:50.963 --> 00:08:52.064
You would not have

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:52.999
I wouldn't have said

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:55.167
an existential threat, because we could.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:56.369
That's too big a word.

00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:59.138
We survive And I'm using

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:00.439
an existential

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:02.041
I'm using a big word

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.409
when it comes to Donald Trump.

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.177
Okay. Fair enough. Fair enough.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.113
To legend some

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.714
of the era and end of today as well.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:09.482
Richard Ben-Veniste

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:10.449
and Bob Woodward, thanks so much

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:12.051
for being here.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:12.685
Really appreciate it.

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:13.352
Good to see you, sir.

